# Apple corners (squircle) in launcher UI

All **Shortcuts / Automation editor** surfaces in `uclient_launcher_ui.h` use **continuous curvature (squircle)**, not plain CSS `border-radius` alone.

## Required pattern

1. Set a generous `border-radius` on the element (blocks ~26px, pills 999px, inset fields ~16–22px).
2. Include the selector in the existing `@supports (corner-shape: squircle)` block so `corner-shape: squircle` applies.

## Must use squircle

- Editor sheet, blocks, drawer, chips, catalog rows, pills, smart menus, run-result boxes, modals, and control surfaces inside `#sc-editor` / `#shortcuts-view`.

## When adding new UI

- Add the new class to the squircle `@supports` list in the same edit.
- Do not ship sharp-corner-only panels in the shortcut editor unless the host OS cannot parse `corner-shape` (fallback remains `border-radius` only).

